## How to read generated AOF state

The project uses distinct dimensions:

```text
Applicability != NormativeLevel != AdoptionState != ImplementationState != VerificationState
```

`planned` means the project intends to adopt a control. `not_assessed` means the CLI has not proven an implementation exists. `not_evaluated` means no conformance/verification result exists.

## Core execution boundary

For consequential operations:

```text
Agent output
-> UntrustedProposal
-> Governance Evaluation
-> AuthorizedDecision
-> ExecutionContract
-> Effect Boundary
-> Effect
-> Evidence
-> Verification
-> Trace
```

Mandatory `Pending` is never implicit Allow.

## Generated governance map

- `.aof/applicability.yaml` — control/object applicability and status dimensions
- `.aof/requirements.yaml` — requirement IDs traced to the canonical specification
- `.aof/provenance.json` — pinned LTS checksums
- `aof/control/` — Safety Kernel and gate mapping
- `aof/architecture/` — Four Planes, Trust Boundaries, Effect Boundaries
- `aof/authority/` — Authority lifecycle and scope
- `aof/policies/` — Policy enforcement/conflict-resolution model
- `aof/risk/` — dynamic Risk and acceptance model
- `aof/execution/` — StateTransition, failure/recovery, consequential effects
- `aof/assurance/` — Evidence, Verification, Trace, accountability
- `aof/conformance/` — scoped adoption and explicit gaps
- `aof/schemas/` — pinned canonical AOF v1.0 LTS JSON Schemas

Canonical upstream: https://github.com/aof-framework/aof
